Interactive USD edits of the per-instance primvars of a point instancer without geometry deduplication

With HDARNOLD_GEOM_DEDUP=0, the prototype of a point instancer is instanced through the instance_matrix of its own
shape node rather than an arnold instancer node. The point instancer gets a per-instance displayColor primvar, edited,
blocked, set again and removed. The stage is re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last render of the procedural is
compared against the reference image.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
